@startuml
title Timeline: rolling trims, copying effects between clips, drag ghost and auto-scroll, muting a video track

actor User
participant TimelineView
participant TimelineEditor
participant "History" as H

== trim a cut between two clips (rolling edit) ==
User -> TimelineView : drag the edge where two clips touch
TimelineView -> TimelineView : BeginRoll: the touching neighbour, and how far the cut can go\n(the neighbour keeps 0.1 s and stays inside its file)
loop pointer moves
  TimelineView -> TimelineView : the trimmed clip's edge moves (clamped)
  TimelineView -> TimelineView : ApplyRoll: the neighbour's edge follows, its in/out point with it
end
note right of TimelineView
  nothing moves on the timeline; an edge with a gap after it
  just trims, up to the next clip (it never pushes)
end note
TimelineView -> TimelineEditor : CommitClipGeometry(both clips): one undo step

== copy and paste effects ==
User -> TimelineView : clip menu, Copy effects\n(or Ctrl+C with effect bars selected)
TimelineView -> TimelineEditor : CopyEffects(clipId) / CopySelected()
note right of TimelineEditor
  effect clipboard: the effect regions over the clip on its track,
  each with its offset from the clip start (or from the earliest bar).
  Kept apart from the clip clipboard; Ctrl+V pastes whichever was copied last.
end note
User -> TimelineView : select other video clips, Paste effects (Ctrl+V)
TimelineView -> TimelineEditor : PasteEffects(clipIds)
loop each target clip
  TimelineEditor -> TimelineEditor : copy each region onto the clip's track at\nclip start + offset, cut to the clip, keyframes moved with it
end
TimelineEditor -> H : one undo step

== drag ghost ==
User -> TimelineView : drag clips
TimelineView -> TimelineView : remember where each clip started
loop pointer moves
  TimelineView -> TimelineView : ghost of every dragged clip where the pointer puts it\n(red when it would land on another clip and can't go)
  TimelineView -> TimelineView : faint outline where they came from
end

== auto-scroll ==
loop every 16 ms while any drag is on and the pointer is near an edge
  TimelineView -> TimelineView : scroll toward that edge, faster the closer it is\n(left/right: time; top/bottom: tracks)
  TimelineView -> TimelineView : replay the last pointer position, so the drag follows
end

== mute a video track ==
User -> TimelineView : speaker button in a video track's header
TimelineView -> TimelineEditor : SetTrackMuted(track, !Muted)
note right : the mixer already skips muted tracks of any kind;\nthe eye still hides the picture
@enduml
